1
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:12,940
A straight road runs from town A at 1, 2 to town B at 13, 8, on a grid in kilometres.

2
00:00:12,990 --> 00:00:18,800
Planners want charging stations one third and two thirds of the way along.

3
00:00:18,850 --> 00:00:21,810
Where is the point one third of the way along?

4
00:00:21,860 --> 00:00:25,300
Pause the video and work it out.

5
00:00:25,350 --> 00:00:27,960
The road goes 12 across and 6 up.

6
00:00:28,010 --> 00:00:30,930
A third of that is 4 across and 2 up.

7
00:00:30,980 --> 00:00:33,420
From 1, 2, that is 5, 4.

8
00:00:33,470 --> 00:00:37,550
Remember: the midpoint of 2, 4 and 8, 10 is 5, 7.

9
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:39,790
It is halfway along.

10
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:43,680
Find the step from A to B: across, 13 minus 1 is 12.

11
00:00:43,730 --> 00:00:45,110
Up, 8 minus 2 is 6.

12
00:00:45,160 --> 00:00:51,120
For a fraction of the way, start at A, and add that fraction of the step.

13
00:00:51,170 --> 00:00:51,790
Your turn.

14
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:54,940
Where is the point two thirds of the way along?

15
00:00:54,990 --> 00:00:58,150
Pause the video and try it.

16
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:00,110
Two thirds of 12 is 8.

17
00:01:00,160 --> 00:01:01,980
Two thirds of 6 is 4.

18
00:01:02,030 --> 00:01:04,670
From 1, 2, that is 9, 6.

19
00:01:04,720 --> 00:01:10,170
A point that divides A B in the ratio 1 to 3 splits it into 4 parts.

20
00:01:10,220 --> 00:01:10,860
Your turn.

21
00:01:10,910 --> 00:01:12,310
Ratio 1 to 3, from A.

22
00:01:12,360 --> 00:01:15,920
Is that a quarter of the way, or a third of the way?

23
00:01:15,970 --> 00:01:19,190
Pause the video and choose.

24
00:01:19,240 --> 00:01:20,780
A quarter of the way.

25
00:01:20,830 --> 00:01:24,430
1 part out of 1 plus 3, which is 4 parts.

26
00:01:24,480 --> 00:01:27,020
Be careful with negative numbers.

27
00:01:27,070 --> 00:01:33,690
From negative 4, 6 to 8, negative 2, the step is 12 across, and negative 8 up.

28
00:01:33,740 --> 00:01:35,020
Here is the method.

29
00:01:35,070 --> 00:01:37,900
Step 1: find the step, B minus A.

30
00:01:37,950 --> 00:01:42,270
Step 2: for a ratio M to N, the fraction is M over M plus N.

31
00:01:42,320 --> 00:01:46,900
Step 3: multiply the step by the fraction, and add it to A.

32
00:01:46,950 --> 00:01:50,440
Step 4: check the point is between A and B.

33
00:01:50,490 --> 00:01:53,270
P divides A B in the ratio 2 to 3.

34
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:55,350
A is 0, 5 and B is 10, 0.

35
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:57,440
The fraction is 2 fifths.

36
00:01:57,490 --> 00:01:59,680
The step is 10, negative 5.

37
00:01:59,730 --> 00:02:02,350
2 fifths of it is 4, negative 2.

38
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:03,980
So P is 4, 3.

39
00:02:04,030 --> 00:02:08,270
M at 5, 4 is one third of the way from A at 2, 1 to B.

40
00:02:08,320 --> 00:02:10,660
One third of the step is 3, 3.

41
00:02:10,710 --> 00:02:14,630
So the whole step is 9, 9, and B is 11, 10.

42
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:18,860
Find the point one third of the way from 3, 3 to 9, 12.

43
00:02:18,910 --> 00:02:19,790
Mia answers.

44
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:21,880
Which line is wrong?

45
00:02:21,930 --> 00:02:22,940
Line 1 is wrong.

46
00:02:22,990 --> 00:02:26,610
Take a third of the step, not of the end point.

47
00:02:26,660 --> 00:02:28,060
The step is 6, 9.

48
00:02:28,110 --> 00:02:29,420
A third is 2, 3.

49
00:02:29,470 --> 00:02:31,250
Add to A: 5, 6.

50
00:02:31,300 --> 00:02:39,250
Animation software places the in-between frames at fractions of the way along a path, so movement looks smooth.

51
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:40,560
One last question.

52
00:02:40,610 --> 00:02:44,880
Where is the point 3 quarters of the way from 0, 0 to 4, 8?

53
00:02:44,930 --> 00:02:48,250
Pause the video and answer.

54
00:02:48,300 --> 00:02:50,230
3 quarters of 4 is 3.

55
00:02:50,280 --> 00:02:52,220
3 quarters of 8 is 6.

56
00:02:52,270 --> 00:02:53,520
So 3, 6.

57
00:02:53,570 --> 00:02:56,290
To remember: the step is B minus A.

58
00:02:56,340 --> 00:03:00,020
The point is A plus the fraction times the step.

59
00:03:00,070 --> 00:03:02,820
Ratio M to N means M over M plus N.

60
00:03:02,870 --> 00:03:05,700
The midpoint is the half-way case.

61
00:03:05,750 --> 00:03:11,150
Great work! Now practise lesson 13.2 on Camday.
